 "version": 2,
 "guide": "Version 2, 26 Sep 2026, written to the coordinator's rules for the M4 retests before the second run: the key is what is CORRECT for Copilot, checked against the model's structure, never what an author happened to leave. EXCLUDE: keys (every column at either end of a relationship, every column marked as a key, and row identifiers such as ids, codes that only identify a row, line numbers and surrogate keys), technical columns (a column whose only job is to set another column's order, audit and load fields, name-style flags, logins, revision numbers, slowly changing dimension bookkeeping such as status, start and end dates and current flags, unit-of-measure codes), pictures and files, helper tables (field parameters), duplicates (a column that repeats a field another table already carries), and a measure named as legacy. INCLUDE: business-facing tables, columns and measures: descriptive attributes, dates and date parts people ask about, standard business codes (currency, country, state, postal), SKUs and order numbers people quote, amounts, quantities and business measures. A date column at the end of a relationship is the date people ask about, and a table's only descriptive column is that table's name: both are included. EITHER (not scored): a calculation group. THE SCHEMA'S OWN RULE WINS: anything an included measure uses is included, because the product refuses to leave it out; the non-live test checks this. Version 1 (commit 65e331f4) was scored in the first run and is kept in git history.",
